# Name mapping from magikos-base.packages, kept here so the next port does not
# re-derive it:
#   bind -> bind9              wpa_supplicant -> wpasupplicant
#   libspa-0.2-jack -> pipewire-jack (the Arch name is frozen at libspa 1.4 and
#     conflicts with the libspa-0.2-modules that current pipewire ships)
#   awesome-terminal-fonts -> fonts-font-awesome
#   alsa-firmware -> alsa-firmware-loaders
#   alsa-plugins -> libasound2-plugins
#   amd-ucode -> amd64-microcode
#   mako -> mako-notifier       nss-mdns -> libnss-mdns       libva-dbus2 -> libva2
#   xorg-xwayland -> xwayland   mkinitramfs -> initramfs-tools
#   ttf-bitstream-vera -> fonts-dejavu-core
#   ttf-liberation -> fonts-liberation
#   ttf-jetbrains-mono-nerd -> fonts-jetbrains-mono
#   poppler-glib -> poppler-utils
#   imv, foot, fuzzel, wmenu, sway*, quickshell, uwsm keep the same names
#
# Dropped, no apt counterpart: every cachyos-* package (CachyOS repo only),
# yay, yay-debug, paru, pacman-contrib, bluetui, pkgfile, reflector, topgrade,
# os-prober, hwdetect, netctl (systemctl owns it), nano-syntax-highlighting,
# mkusb, swaync, ttf-ms-fonts (ttf-mscorefonts-installer is non-free),
# wl-clipboard-wayland (covered by wl-clipboard), base, base-devel, libvpl,
# vpl-gpu-rt, egl-wayland, libpulse, qml6-module-plain-text-model (Qt-version
# dependent).
#
# Also omitted: the openssh split (openssh-client/-server/-sftp-server). Debian
# ties the server to an exact openssh-client version, so on a host whose client
# came from backports the transaction is unsatisfiable and apt attempts a
# downgrade it refuses -- it cost two failures out of every install. Nothing in
# the session needs it. The Arch list keeps openssh; a Debian adopter who wants
# a remote shell installs it themselves, or pulls openssh-server from
# backports so it matches their client.
#
# Shipped as pinned upstream binaries by the installer instead, because neither
# repository carries them: topgrade (magikos-update) and oh-my-posh.